# A 2D SiC monolayer, 2 atoms/cell (1 Si + 1 C), already relaxed at its DFT
# equilibrium in-plane lattice constant (vacuum along z, Lz ~ 20.77 Ang).
# Chosen on purpose, same spirit as 4.1-strain's cubic Si: its point group,
# -6m2 (hexagonal, non-centrosymmetric), makes stb-elasticInputs'
# --symmetry-method basic/full distinction REAL, not a toy illustration --
# 'basic' needs all 3 in-plane directions (15 SIESTA calculations at the
# strain range this example uses) to fully determine the stiffness matrix,
# while 'full' needs only 1 (5 calculations) for the exact same physics.
# See the README's worked example (section 4) for the real numbers.

NumberOfSpecies    2
NumberofAtoms      2

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   14   Si
 2   6   C
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 1.55197287   -2.68805717   -0.00000001
 1.55197287   2.68805717   0.00000001
 -0.00000000   0.00000010   20.76959437
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  -0.00001187   0.00001187   0.29543400   1
  0.66667911   0.33332089   0.29543631   2
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
